CHAPTER I GENERAL PROVISIONS

Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters mandated by the Mountainous Districts Management Act and matters necessary for its enforcement. <Amended on Aug. 5, 2005; Apr. 20, 2009>

Article 2 (Land excluded from mountainous districts) In the proviso, with the exception of the items, of subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Mountainous Districts Management Act (hereinafter referred to as "the Act"), "farmland, grassland, roads, and other land prescribed by Presidential Decree" means the land that falls under any of the following subparagraphs: <Amended on Aug. 5, 2005; Dec. 7, 2010; Jun. 1, 2015; Jun. 2, 2017; Jul. 2, 2019, Aug. 19, 2020>
  1. Land the category of which under Article 67(1) of the Act on the Establishment and Management of Spatial Information (hereinafter referred to as "land classification") is classified as a field, paddy field, orchard, or ranch land (limited to land that has been created as pasture for livestock farming and dairy farming under subparagraph 4a of Article 58 of the Enforcement Decree of that Act);
  2. Land the category of which is road; provided, the land where standing trees and bamboo are growing collectively and which has lost its function as a road shall be excluded;
  3. Land the category of which is an embankment, ditch, or puddle;
  4. Rivers under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the River Act;
  5. Land the category of which is not forest land, which falls under the following items:
  a. Tea plantations, or fields for gathering cuttings or scions;
  b. Land within the building fence;
  c. Ridge of rice paddies or fields;
  6. Land classified as forest land in category, which is being used for purposes other than forest land after being exempted from the obligation to restore the land under Article 39(3)2 of the Act or undergoing a completion inspection for restoration under Article 42 of the Act, after obtaining permission for the conversion of mountainous districts under Article 14 of the Act or notification of the conversion of mountainous districts under Article 15 of the Act (including cases where permission or notification for conversion is deemed to have been granted pursuant to other statutes).

Article 3 (Cultivation of forest products excluded from conversion of mountainous districts) "Forest products prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 2c of Article 2 of the Act refers to the items eligible for support as income sources of forest products under Article 8(1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Forestry and Mountain Villages Development Promotion Act.
  [This Article Added on Jun. 2, 2017]

CHAPTER II CONSERVATION OF MOUNTAINOUS DISTRICTS

SECTION 1 Master Plans for Management of Mountainous Districts and Classification of Mountainous Districts

Article 3-2 (Public notice of master plan for management of mountainous districts) When the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service formulates or amends a master plan for the management of mountainous districts under Article 3-2(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "master plan"), he or she shall publicly notify the following matters under Article 3-2(7) of the Act: <Amended on Jun. 2, 2020>
  1. In cases of formulating a master plan: Outline and main content of the formulated master plan;
  2. In cases of modifying the master plan: Content of the modified master plan.
  [This Article Added on Dec. 7, 2010]

Article 3-3 (Matters to be included in master plans and regional plans) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 3-3(1)6 of the Act refers to the following matters:
  1. Matters related to an area subject to restrictions on conversion or temporary use of mountainous districts under Article 9(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "restricted areas for conversion and temporary use of mountainous districts");
  2. Matters related to the prohibited areas for extraction of earth and stones under Article 25-3(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "prohibited areas for extraction of earth and stones");
  3. Matters related to the designation of a quarry complex under Article 29(1) of the Act;
  4. Matters related to the stable supply of stone;
  5. Matters related to the restoration and recovery of mountainous districts;
  6. Matters related to linkage with forestry-related administrative plans under other statutes;
  7. Matters related to the promotion of projects related to the conservation and use of mountainous districts and their financial resources.
  [This Article Added on Dec. 7, 2010]

Article 3-4 (Survey for formulation of master plan and regional plan) (1) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 3-4(1) of the Act means any of the following cases:
  1. In cases the master plan is modified due to changes in forestry-related administrative plans according to other statutes;
  2. In cases where the master plan can be modified by utilizing the results of the mountainous district survey (hereinafter referred to as "regional survey of mountainous districts") under the main clause of Article 3-4(2) of the Act.
  (2) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 3-4(2) of the Act means any of the following cases: <Amended on Jun. 2, 2020>
  1. In cases where the regional plans for the management of mountainous districts under Article 3-2(8) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "regional plan") are modified in line with modifications of forestry-related administrative plans under other statutes;
  2. In cases where regional plans may be formulated or modified by utilizing the results of basic survey on mountainous districts under the main clause of Article 3-4(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "basic survey on mountainous districts");
  3. In cases where the regional plans are modified due to any changes in the administrative plans related to land use under other statutes and regulations.
  (3) In Article 3-4(3) of the Act, "other institutions prescribed by Presidential Decree" means the Korea Forest Disaster Safety Technology Corporation under Article 58 of the Forest Disaster Prevention Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Korea Forest Disaster Safety Technology Corporation"). <Amended on Dec. 30, 2016; Dec. 16, 2021; Jan. 30, 2026>
  [This Article Added on Dec. 7, 2010]

Article 3-5 (Establishment and operation of mountainous district management information system) (1) The information system on the management of mountainous districts under Article 3-5(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "mountainous district management information system") shall include the following: <Amended on Aug. 22, 2012>
  1. Matters related to the basic survey on mountainous districts and the regional survey on mountainous districts;
  2. Matters related to the classification of mountainous districts under Article 4 of the Act;
  3. Matters related to restricted areas for the conversion and temporary use of mountainous districts, as well as restricted areas for earth and stone extraction;
  4. Matters related to administrative dispositions related to the conversion and temporary use of mountainous districts, earth and stone extraction, and mountainous district restoration, etc.;
  5. Other information related to the conservation and use of mountainous districts, as determined by the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service.
  (2) The electronic information processing system under Article 3-5(2) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "integrated information system for conversion of mountainous districts") shall include each of the following matters: <Added on Dec. 16, 2021>
  1. Matters related to permission for conversion of mountainous districts under Article 14 of the Act and notification of conversion of mountainous districts under Article 15 of the Act;
  2. Matters related to permission and notification for temporary use of mountainous districts under Article 15-2 of the Act;
  3. Matters related to substitute forest resource development charges under Article 19 of the Act;
  4. Matters related to permission to extract earth and stones and notification of extraction of earth and sand under Article 25 of the Act;
  5. Matters related to designation and revocation of quarry districts under Article 29 of the Act and quarrying notification under Article 30 of the Act;
  6. Matters related to the sale of earth and stones from mountainous districts within State forest under Article 35 of the Act;
  7. Matters related to restoration of converted mountainous districts under Article 39 of the Act;
  8. Other matters determined by the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service to efficiently process the affairs of management of mountainous districts.
  (3) The Administrator of the Korea Forest Service may request the heads of the relevant administrative agencies to submit necessary data, if deemed necessary to establish and operate an information system for management of mountainous districts. In such cases, the head of the administrative agency in receipt of such request shall comply therewith, unless there is a justifiable reason. <Amended on Aug. 22, 2012; Dec. 16, 2021>
  (4) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (3), detailed matters necessary for establishing and operating the information mountainous district management information system and the integrated information system for conversion of mountainous districts shall be determined by the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service. <Amended on Dec. 16, 2021>
  (5) "A specialized institution for mountainous districts prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 3-5(4) of the Act means the Korea Forest Conservation Association under Article 46(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "KFCA"). <Added on Aug. 22, 2012; Dec. 16, 2021>
  (6) Where the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service entrusts the establishment and operation of an information system for management of mountainous districts under Article 3-5(4) of the Act, he or she shall fully or partially subsidize the entrusted person for expenses incurred in performing the entrusted affairs within budgetary limits. <Added on Aug. 22, 2012; Dec. 16, 2021>
  [This Article Added on Dec. 7, 2010]

Article 4 (Classification of mountainous districts) (1) "Mountainous districts prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 4(1)1a4) of the Act means any of the following mountainous districts not designated or determined as the area, district, zone, etc. (hereinafter referred to as "the areas, etc.") to be conserved or used for specific purposes under other statutes: <Amended on Aug. 5, 2005; Aug. 4, 2006; Dec. 7, 2010; May 29, 2017>
  1. Mountainous districts clustered as a natural forest or artificial forest with excellent characteristics;
  2. Mountainous districts with fertile soil suitable for the growth of trees;
  3. State forests other than conservation State forests under Article 16(1)1 of the Act on the State Forest Administration and Management Act, where forests are aggregated into contiguous areas;
  4. Mountainous districts that the head of a local government intends to use for forest management purposes;
  5. Other mountainous districts for laying the foundation for forestry production and efficiently producing forest products.
  (2) "Green areas prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 4(1)1b9) of the Act means green conservation areas referred to in Article 30(1)4a of the Enforcement Decree of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act. <Amended on Dec. 7, 2010; Mar. 11, 2025>
  (3) In Article 4(1)1b15) of the Act, "mountainous districts prescribed by Presidential Decree" means any of the following mountainous districts: <Amended on Dec. 7, 2010; Sep. 25, 2015; Dec. 29, 2017; Oct. 30, 2018; Jul. 2, 2019; Mar. 3, 2020>
  1. Mountainous districts in natural environment conservation areas under Article 36(1)4 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
  2. Mountainous districts in disaster prevention areas according to Article 37(1)4 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
  3. Mountainous districts in urban natural park areas under Article 38-2(1) of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
  4. Mountainous districts within the fishery resource protection zones under Article 40 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
  5. Mountainous districts within natural scenic districts, historical and cultural environment protection districts, and ecosystem protection districts under Article 31(2)1a, and subparagraph 5a and c of that paragraph of the Enforcement Decree of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
  6. Mountainous districts necessary for the protection of forest ecosystem, mountainous landscape, coastal landscape, coastal sand dunes, or living environments;
  7. Mountainous districts that the head of a central administrative agency or the head of a local government intends to use for public interest purposes.
  [Title Amended on Jul. 24, 2008]

Article 5 (Public notice of designation and revocation of conservation mountainous districts) (1) Where the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service has designated conservation mountainous districts under Article 5(1) of the Act, he or she shall publicly notify the following: <Amended on Jul. 24, 2008>
  1. The number and title of the topographic map, at a scale of 1:25,000 or larger, indicating the area of the conservation mountainous districts, with cadastral boundaries marked (in cases where a cadastral-marked topographic map under Article 12 of the Framework Act on the Regulation of Land Use has not been established in the national land use information system, or where discrepancies between topography and cadastral boundaries make it difficult to utilize the topographic map, a cadastral map may be used instead);
  2. The title of administrative district included in the area of conservation mountainous districts.
  (2) Where the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service intends to modify or revoke the designation of a conservation mountainous district under Article 6(4) of the Act, he or she shall publicly notify the following: <Amended on Jul. 24, 2008>
  1. The number and the title of the drawing of the topographic map, at a scale of 1:25,000 or larger, showing the boundaries of the conservation mountainous districts to be modified or the designation of which is revoked, with cadastral information indicated (if a database of topographic maps with cadastral markings under Article 12 of the Framework Act on the Regulation of Land Use has not been established in the national land use information system, or if it is difficult to use the topographic map due to discrepancies between the topography and the cadastral information, a cadastral map may be used instead);
  2. Name of the administrative district included in the conservation mountainous districts, the designation of which is modified or revoked.

Article 6 (Procedures for consultation on designation and determination of the areas, etc. in mountainous districts) (1) The head of a relevant administrative agency who intends to consult with the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, a Metropolitan City Mayor, a Special Self-Governing City Mayor, a Do Governor, a Special Self-Governing Province Governor (hereinafter referred to as "Mayor/Do Governor"), or the head of a Si (referring to a Special Self- Governing City Mayor in cases of a Special Self-Governing City, and a Special Self-Governing Province Governor in cases of a Special Self-Governing Province in which no Si/Gun that is a local government exists within its jurisdiction; hereinafter the same shall apply), Gun/Gu (referring to an autonomous Gu; hereinafter the same shall apply) in accordance with Article 8(1) of the Act shall submit a written request for consultation along with documents prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs to the following persons: <Amended on Aug. 22, 2012; Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 2, 2017; Jun. 7, 2023>
  1. Where the area of mountainous districts (referring to the area of mountainous districts to be modified, excluding the area already agreed upon, in cases where consultation on modification is sought under the latter part of Article 8(1) of the Act; hereinafter the same shall apply in this subparagraph) is 2,000,000 square meters or more (1,000,000 square meters or more in the case of conservation mountainous districts): The Administrator of the Korea Forest Service;
  2. Where the area of mountainous districts is 500,000 square meters or more but less than 2 million square meters (in case of conservation mountainous districts, 30,000 square meters or more but less than 1 million square meters):
  a. In cases of mountainous districts in the State forests under the jurisdiction of the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service: The Administrator of the Korea Forest Service;
  b. In cases of mountainous districts in the State forest, public forest, or private forest not under the jurisdiction of the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service: Mayor/Do Governor;
  3. Where the area of mountainous districts is less than 500,000 square meters (less than 30,000 square meters in the case of conservation mountainous districts):
  a. In cases of mountainous districts in the State forests under the jurisdiction of the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service: The Administrator of the Korea Forest Service;
  b. In cases of mountainous districts within State forest, public forest, or private forest not under the jurisdiction of the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service: The head of a Si/Gun/Gu.
  (2) "Minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 8(1) of the Act means any of the following matters: In such cases, the head of the relevant administrative agency shall, without delay, notify the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, a Mayor/Do Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu (hereinafter referred to as the "Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, etc.") of details of the changed lot number, land category, and area of the mountainous district: <Amended on Jul. 24, 2008; Nov. 26, 2009; Dec. 14, 2009; Dec. 7, 2010; Aug. 22, 2012; Jun. 1, 2015>
  1. Reducing the surface area of the areas, etc. designated or determined by the head of the relevant administrative agency in consultation with the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, etc.;
  2. An increase or decrease in the surface area of the areas, etc. etc. without changing its district as a result of a split survey conducted under Article 79 of the Act on the Establishment and Management of Spatial Data;
  3. Deleted. <Dec. 7, 2010>
  [Title Amended on Jul. 27, 2007]

Article 7 (Notification of consultation on designation and determination of the areas, etc. in mountainous districts) (1) The scope of the areas, etc. that the heads of relevant administrative agencies shall consult with the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, etc. in accordance with Article 8(1) of the Act shall be as specified in Appendix 1. <Amended on Aug. 22, 2012>
  (2) Upon receipt of a request from the head of a relevant administrative agency for consultation on the designation or determination of the areas, etc. in mountainous districts under Article 8(1) of the Act, the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, etc. shall conduct a field survey on the relevant mountainous districts, examine the matters for which consultation is requested in accordance with the criteria specified in Appendix 2, and notify his or her opinion; provided, the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, etc. may, if the head of a relevant administrative agency has undergone a feasibility survey on conversion of mountainous districts under Article 18-2(1) of the Act, examine it without conducting a field survey. <Amended on Jul. 27, 2007; Aug. 22, 2012; Dec. 31, 2014>
  (3) If necessary for examining matters for which consultation is requested under paragraph (2), the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, etc. may hear opinions of a Mayor/Do Governor, the head of a Regional Forest Service, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu, or the head of State Forest Management Office under Regional Forest Service (hereinafter referred to as "the head of State Forest Management Office") in connection with the matters for which consultation is requested. <Added on Dec. 17, 2013>
  (4) A person who has received a request for submission of opinions under paragraph (3) from the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, etc. shall submit his or her opinion to the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, etc. within 15 days from the date of receiving the request, unless there is a justifiable reason not to do so. <Added on Dec. 17, 2013; Dec. 31, 2014>
  (5) In cases where the request for consultation under paragraph (2) falls under any of the following subparagraphs, the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service or the Mayor/Do Governor shall undergo deliberation by the Central Mountainous District Management Committee under Article 22(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Central Mountainous District Management Committee") or the Regional Forest Management Committee under paragraph (2) of that Article (hereinafter referred to as the "Regional Forest Management Committee"): <Amended on Dec. 7, 2010; Aug. 22, 2012>
  1. In cases where the area of the conservation mountainous district incorporated into the areas, etc. subject to consultation is 2 million square meters or more;
  2. In cases where the area of the conservation mountainous district incorporated into a tourist resort facility or sports facility is 500,000 square meters or more.
  [Title Amended on Jul. 27, 2007]

SECTION 2 Restrictions on Acts within Conservation Mountainous Districts

Article 8 (Mountainous districts subject to designation as restricted areas for conversion and temporary use of mountainous districts) (1) In Article 9(1)1 of the Act, "main mountain ranges prescribed by Presidential Decree" means any of the following mountain ranges: <Amended on Mar. 11, 2025>
  1. Baekdudaegan defined in subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Baekdu-Daegan Protection Act;
  2. Main ridges as prescribed in each subparagraph of Article 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Baekdu-Daegan Protection Act;
  3. Other mountain ranges designated and publicly notified by the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service as necessary for the conservation of mountainous landscapes and forest ecosystems.
  (2) Mountainous districts of a mountain range referred to in Article 9(1)1 of the Act, which are necessary for the conservation of mountain landscape and forest ecosystem, shall be mountainous districts located within a horizontal distance of 1 kilometer to either side from the central ridgeline of the relevant mountain range; provided, the mountainous district falling under any of the following subparagraphs shall be excluded: <Amended on Aug. 5, 2005; Dec. 7, 2010; Oct. 30, 2018>
  1. Mountainous districts that are deemed inappropriate to be designated as a restricted area for conversion or temporary use of mountainous districts in consideration of topography, conditions of land use in the vicinity, etc.;
  2. Mountainous districts in which development is underway for other purposes with authorization, permission, approval, etc. obtained under other statutes or regulations or development plans are finalized;
  3. Mountainous districts of Baekdu-daegan Protection Areas under Article 6 of the Baekdu-Daegan Protection Act.
  (3) In Article 9(1)2 of the Act, "mountainous districts prescribed by Presidential Decree" means any of the following mountainous districts: <Amended on Dec. 7, 2010; Oct. 30, 2018; May 7, 2024>
  1. Mountainous districts with high academic, artistic, and scenic value as a mountain landscape;
  2. Mountainous districts related to historical facts or historical figures;
  3. Mountainous districts necessary for the protection of national heritage, such as traditional temples and monuments;
  4. Mountainous districts necessary for conservation for the improvement of public health, recreation, and healing.
  (4) In Article 9(1)3 of the Act, "mountainous districts prescribed by Presidential Decree" means the following mountainous districts: <Amended on Jul. 27, 2007; Feb. 29, 2008; Dec. 7, 2010; Mar. 23, 2013>
  1. Mountainous districts in which landslides are highly likely to occur, depending on risk factors specified in the standards for determining landslide risk areas prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs, such as the gradient, mother rock, and forest conditions of the mountainous districts;
  2. Mountainous districts highly susceptible to soil erosion due to heavy rainfall or other similar events.
  [Title Amended on Dec. 7, 2010]

Article 9 (Procedures for designation of restricted areas for conversion or temporary use of mountainous districts) (1) Where the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service intends to hear opinions from the owners of the relevant mountainous districts, etc. under Article 9(2) of the Act, he or she shall give prior notice thereof to the owners of the relevant mountainous districts, publicly announce the lot number, land category, area, etc. of the areas to be designated as the restricted areas for the conversion or temporary use of mountainous districts in the Official Gazette, and widely publicize it through newspapers, broadcasting, the Internet, and other methods. <Amended on Dec. 7, 2010; Aug. 22, 2012>
  (2) Where the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service has publicly announced the parcel number, land category, area, etc. of a prearranged area for designation as a restricted area for conversion or temporary use of a mountainous district in the Official Gazette under paragraph (1), he or she shall require the head of the competent Si/Gun/Gu or the Director of the competent National Forest Management Office to make the land specification indicating the parcel number, land category, area, etc. of the mountainous district to be incorporated into the restricted area for conversion or temporary use of a mountainous district, as well as a topographic map indicating a scale of at least 1:25,000 (or a cadastral map, if the database of topographic maps indicating the land category is not constructed in the national land use information system under Article 12 of the Framework Act on the Regulation of Land Use, or if it is difficult to utilize topographic maps due to discrepancies between topography and cadastre) available to make it available to the public for inspection for at least 20 days. <Amended on Aug. 5, 2005; Jul. 24, 2008; Dec. 7, 2010; Aug. 22, 2012; Dec. 17, 2013>
  (3) A person who intends to present his or her opinion on the details of public inspection under paragraph (2) shall submit a written opinion (including a written opinion in electronic form) to the head of the competent Si/Gun/Gu or the head of State Forest Management Office within 30 days from the date the public inspection commences. <Amended on Mar. 17, 2004>
  (4) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu or the head of State Forest Management Office in receipt of opinions submitted under paragraph (3) shall examine the validity of the details of opinions and submit the results thereof to a Mayor/Do Governor or the head of a Regional Forest Service, and the Mayor/Do Governor or the head of Regional Forest Service shall submit the results thereof to the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, along with his or her comprehensive opinions. <Amended on Jan. 26, 2006>
  (5) In cases where the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service designates a restricted area from the conversion or temporary use of mountainous districts under Article 9(3) of the Act, the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service shall publicly notify the following: <Amended on Jul. 24, 2008; Dec. 7, 2010>
  1. The number and title of the topographic map, at a scale of 1:25,000 or larger, indicating the area of the restricted areas for conversion or temporary use of mountainous districts, with cadastral boundaries marked (in cases where a cadastral-marked topographic map under Article 12 of the Framework Act on the Regulation of Land Use has not been established in the national land use information system, or where discrepancies between topography and cadastral boundaries make it difficult to utilize the topographic map, a cadastral map may be used instead);
  2. Names of administrative districts included in restricted areas for conversion or temporary use of mountainous districts.
  [Title Amended on Dec. 7, 2010]

Article 10 (Permitted activities in restricted areas for conversion or temporary use of mountainous districts) (1) "Facilities for official or public use prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 3 of Article 10 of the Act means any of the following facilities: <Amended on Aug. 5, 2005; Feb. 1, 2007; Nov. 2, 2009; Nov. 26, 2009; Dec. 7, 2010; Aug. 22, 2012; Jul. 20, 2015; Dec. 30, 2016; Nov. 24, 2020; Jan. 6, 2022>
  1. Track facilities installed by the State or local governments;
  2. Windbreak facilities or fire prevention facilities;
  3. Meteorological facilities under subparagraph 13 of Article 2 of the Weather Act and observatories under subparagraph 6 of Article 2 of the Act on Observation and Warning of Earthquakes, Tsunamis, and Volcanic Eruptions;
  4. Government office buildings established by the State or local governments;
  5. Trails, observatories, and shelters installed within natural parks pursuant to the Natural Parks Act, as well as protective and safety facilities intended to ensure the safety of visitors;
  6. Natural environment conservation and utilization facilities under the Natural Environment Conservation Act;
  7. Natural recreation forests, forest bathing areas, healing forests, children's forest experience centers, forest ecology centers, forest paths including walking trails, exploration routes, hiking trails, observatories (including pavilions), and shelters established by the State or local governments;
  8. National arboretums and arboretum facilities established with approval of the arboretum establishment plan under Article 7 of the Act on the Creation and Furtherance of Arboretums and Gardens;
  9. National communications facilities or telecommunications facilities under subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Framework Act on Telecommunications;
  10. Waterworks facilities under subparagraph 17 of Article 3 of the Water Supply and Waterworks Installation Act;
  11. Sewerage systems under subparagraph 3 of Article 2 of the Sewerage Act;
  12. Groundwater measurement facilities under Article 17(1) of the Groundwater Act.
  (2) "Facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 4 of Article 10 of the Act means any of the following facilities: <Amended on Aug. 5, 2005; Aug. 4, 2006; Mar. 9, 2010; Dec. 7, 2010; Dec. 31, 2014; Dec. 30, 2016; Jan. 30, 2026>
  1. Facilities for the control and prevention of pests and diseases;
  2. Facilities for the prevention and recovery from forest disasters such as forest fires and landslides;
  3. Facilities for the conservation and management of veteran trees designated under Article 13(1) of the Forest Protection Act as well as wild flora and fauna;
  4. Forest seedling production facilities (only applicable to those established by the State or local governments);
  5. Forest roads installed in accordance with Article 9(1) of the Creation and Management of Forest Resources Act;
  6. Work roads and forest product transport roads installed by the State or a non-state entity in accordance with a forestry management plan authorized under Article 13(2) of the Creation and Management of Forest Resources Act.
  (3) "Facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 10(5) of the Act means facilities established by any of the following institutions or organizations for the purpose of conducting forestry-related testing and research or achieving educational goals related to forestry: <Amended on Aug. 5, 2005; Dec. 7, 2010>
  1. Forestry testing and research institutes affiliated with the Korea Forest Service (including its affiliated organizations);
  2. Forestry testing and research institutes affiliated with local governments;
  3. A school that has a department or faculty related to forestry as defined in Article 2 of the Higher Education Act.
  (4) "Facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 7 of Article 10 of the Act means the following facilities: <Amended on Aug. 12, 2014>
  1. Power generation facilities;
  2. Substation facilities (including conversion facilities);
  3. Transmission facilities;
  4. Distribution facilities;
  5. Wind and weather measurement facilities.
  (5) "Underground mining prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 8 of Article 10 of the Act means drift mining where the area of temporary use of a mountainous district, including adits and facilities for sorting and processing minerals, is less than 100,000 square meters. <Added on Dec. 7, 2010; Jun. 7, 2023>
  (6) "Investigation and excavation of remains prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 9-3 of Article 10 of the Act means investigation and excavation that falls under any of the following subparagraphs: <Added on Aug. 22, 2012>
  1. Investigation and excavation of the remains of fallen soldiers in accordance with the Act on the Excavation of the Remains of Soldiers Killed in the Korean War;
  2. Investigation and excavation of the remains of victims, etc. in accordance with the Special Act on Verification and Support for the Victims of Forced Mobilization under Japanese Colonialism in Korea;
  3. Other investigations and excavations of remains conducted directly by the State or local governments for the purpose of discovering the remains of missing persons, crime victims, etc.
  (7) "Period prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 10 of Article 10 of the Act means a period not exceeding 1 year; provided, if the period of conversion or temporary use of mountainous districts for carrying out the intended project exceeds 1 year, it means the period of conversion or temporary use of the mountainous district. <Added on Dec. 7, 2010; Aug. 22, 2012>
  (8) In subparagraph 11 of Article 10 of the Act, "access roads below the scale prescribed by Presidential Decree" means access roads with an effective width of 4 meters or less and a length of 50 meters or less, excluding cut-and-fill slopes (slopes formed by cutting or filling). <Added on Dec. 7, 2010; Aug. 22, 2012; Jul. 2, 2019; Nov. 24, 2020>
  [Title Amended on Dec. 7, 2010]

Article 11 (Revocation of designation of restricted areas for conversion or temporary use of mountainous districts) In Article 11(1)4 of the Act, "cases prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as changes in natural, social, economic, or regional conditions, or reasons of regional development" means any of the following cases: <Amended on Jul. 24, 2008; April 20, 2009; Nov. 26, 2009; Dec. 15, 2009; Dec. 7, 2010>
  1. In cases where the head of relevant local government requests the revocation of designation of a restricted area for conversion or temporary use of mountainous districts, because it is deemed necessary to install the facilities permitted in the conservation mountainous districts under Article 12 of the Act, in consideration of local conditions and mountainous characteristics;
  2. In cases where it is necessary for the purpose of living environment improvement projects under subparagraph 10 of Article 2 of the Agricultural and Fishing Villages Improvement Act or mountain village development projects under Article 25 of the Forestry and Mountain Villages Development Promotion Act, and the area included in the project plan site is less than 30/100;
  3. In cases where it is necessary to rationalize land use, such as the installation of infrastructure for regional development (only applicable to transportation facilities, logistics facilities, and information and communication facilities);
  4. In cases where a restricted area for conversion or temporary use of mountainous districts is cut off to less than 3,000 square meters due to the installation of public facilities such as roads and railways;
  5. In cases of establishing a national cemetery under Article 3 of the Act on the Establishment and Management of National Cemeteries;
