  (4) Upon receipt of a request for consultation under paragraph (3), the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall submit the findings of an on-site investigation and their opinions on the possibility of designating a quarry complex to the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service or a Mayor/Do Governor within 15 days, unless there is good cause not to do so. <Added on Aug. 22, 2012; Sep. 24, 2014>
  (5) In Article 29(2) of the Act, "area prescribed by Presidential Decree" means 21/100 of the area designated as a quarry complex. <Added on Aug. 22, 2012; Sep. 24, 2014; Jun. 7, 2023>
  (6) The detailed designation criteria for quarry complexes under Article 29 (3) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on Aug. 5, 2005; Jul. 27, 2007; Apr. 20, 2009; Nov. 26, 2009; May 22, 2012; Aug. 22, 2012; Sep. 24, 2014; Dec. 31, 2014; Dec. 30, 2016; Nov. 24, 2020; Jan. 7, 2025>
  1. The area of one complex shall be 200,000 square meters or more, and rocks shall be distributed collectively. In such cases, if a new quarry complex is to be designated, including an area where rocks have already been excavated and extracted with a quarry excavation permit or a designated quarry complex, the area of the complex shall be calculated including the area of the quarry excavation permit site or the area of the quarry complex, but the area where excavation and extraction have been completed and the area of auxiliary facilities such as product processing facilities shall be excluded;
  2. The area shall have high economic value for collective extraction of rocks and shall not be hindered by the construction of infrastructure such as roads;
  3. It shall not significantly harm the living environment of local residents due to water quality, dust, vibration, noise, etc.;
  4. There shall be neither development plans nor restrictions under other statutes or regulations;
  5. There shall be no rights established in accordance with relevant statues or regulations in the area applied for; provided, this shall not apply if the consent of the person who established the rights has been obtained;
  6. It shall have been evaluated under the Environmental Impact Assessment Act (limited to cases subject to evaluation);
  6-2. The land shall not be a mountainous district falling under Article 25-3(1)1, 4, or 5 of the Act; provided, this shall not apply where any of the following items applies:
  a. Where the land constitutes a mountainous district falling under Article 25-3(1)1 or 4 of the Act (limited to mountainous districts falling under subparagraph 4 of Article 32-3(1) or subparagraph 4 of Article 32-3(3) of this Decree), and consent has been obtained pursuant to Article 32-4(3)1 from the administrative agency or manager of the areas or facilities falling under Article 32-3(1)4 or Article 32-3(3)4;
  b. Where any of the following subitems applies and consent has been obtained from the competent Mayor/Do Governor and the head of the competent Si/Gun/Gu with jurisdiction over a mountainous district falling under Article 25-3(1)5 of the Act that is included in a quarry complex to be designated or re-designated (where such mountainous district is a State forest, referring to the head of the competent Regional Forest Service and the head of the competent National Forest Management Office):
  1) Where a quarry complex is to be designated pursuant to Article 29(1) of the Act [limited to cases where all or part of an area for which permission for extraction of earth and stone has been granted pursuant to Article 25(1) of the Act (including areas where the permission period has expired and restoration is underway or has been completed) is included in the quarry complex to be designated], and where part of the mountainous district to be designated as a quarry complex constitutes a mountainous district falling under Article 25-3(1)5 of the Act;
  2) Where a quarry complex is to be redesignated to expand its area pursuant to Article 29 (1) of the Act, and all or part of the area to be expanded constitutes a mountainous district falling under Article 25-3 (1) 5 of the Act;
  7. The area shall meet the criteria for permission to extract earth and stones under Article 28(1)2 through 6, and paragraph (2) of that Article;
  8. Deleted. <Jun. 2, 2020>
  (7) Where the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service or a Mayor/Do Governor designates a quarry complex or modifies such designation under paragraph (3), they shall manage the quarry complex, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Aug. 22, 2012; Mar. 23, 2013; Sep. 24, 2014>
  (8) Except as otherwise provided in paragraphs (1) through (7), matters necessary for the designation, designation for modification, or management of quarry complexes shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Aug. 22, 2012; Mar. 23, 2013; Sep. 24, 2014>

Article 40 (Notification of quarrying in quarry complex) Any person who wishes to file a notification to excavate or extract rocks from a quarry complex in accordance with Article 30(5) of the Act shall be equipped with the equipment and technical personnel in accordance with Article 36(4). <Amended on Jul. 27, 2007>

Article 41 (Revocation of earth and stones extraction permit) The detailed criteria for the revocation of permission to extract earth and stones, or for the suspension of earth and stones extraction or quarrying, etc. under Article 31(2) of the Act shall be as specified in Appendix 8-3.
