CHAPTER IV PREVENTION OF AND RECOVERY FROM DISASTERS

Article 45 (Prevention of disasters) (1) The Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, etc. may perform the following acts toward a person conducting the conversion and temporary use of mountainous districts, earth and stones extraction (hereinafter referred to as "mountainous district conversion, etc.") or restoration for the purpose of investigation, inspection, and examination under Article 37(1) of the Act: <Amended on Aug. 22, 2012; Oct. 30, 2018; Jan. 30, 2026>
  1. Request for report;
  2. Request for submission of data;
  3. Entry into mountainous districts;
  4. Other acts deemed necessary by the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service for the purpose of preventing forest disasters and maintaining the landscape of mountainous districts.
  (2) In the former part of Article 37(2), "inspection agency prescribed by Presidential Decree" means the Korea Forest Conservation Association and the Korea Forest Disaster Safety Technology Corporation (hereafter referred to as "inspection agency" in paragraphs (3) and (5)). <Added on Jun. 2, 2020; Aug. 19, 2020; Dec. 16, 2021; Jan. 30, 2026>
  (3) The inspection agency shall conduct an investigation, inspection, examination, etc. (hereinafter referred to as "investigation, etc.") by means of a written investigation or on-site inspection in accordance with the former part of Article 37(2) of the Act. <Added on Jun. 2, 2020; Aug. 19, 2020>
  (4) The investigation, etc. shall be conducted at least once every year from the commencement date of construction of new and renewable energy facilities in accordance with the Act on the Promotion of the Development, Use and Diffusion of New and Renewable Energy until the date three years elapse from the notification of the commencement of the project under Article 9(4) of the Electric Utility Act. <Added on Jun. 2, 2020>
  (5) An inspection agency entrusted with conducting investigation, etc. under the former part of Article 37(2) of the Act shall submit the results of such investigation, etc. within 30 days from the date of completion of the investigation, etc. to the holder of the mountainous district conversion permit or temporary use permit, and the permit holder shall, within 7 days from the date of receipt of the results, submit the results to the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, etc. <Added on Jun. 2, 2020; Aug. 19, 2020>
  (6) The management plan for solar power generation facilities (hereinafter referred to as "mountain solar power generation facilities") under subparagraph 2a of Article 2 of the Act on the Promotion of the Development, Use and Diffusion of New and Renewable Energy in accordance with Article 37(3) of the Act shall include the following matters: <Added on Aug. 19, 2020>
  1. Current status of installation and management of mountain solar power generation facilities;
  2. Status of disasters and forest damage caused by the installation of mountain solar power generation facilities;
  3. Disaster prevention measures and mountainous district restoration measures (including management plans for the mountainous district solar power generation facilities);
  4. Plans for inspecting the implementation of management plans for mountain solar power generation facilities;
  5. Other matters deemed necessary by the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, etc. for disaster prevention and mountainous district restoration.
  (7) In Article 37(6) of the Act, "specialized mountainous district institution prescribed by Presidential Decree" means the Korea Forest Conservation Association and the Korea Forest Disaster Safety Technology Corporation. <Added on Dec. 16, 2021; Jan. 30, 2026>
  (8) Where the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, etc. orders necessary measures in accordance with the main clause of Article 37(7) of the Act, they she shall notify in writing the details and period of such measures, etc. <Amended on Aug. 22, 2012; Jun. 2, 2020; Aug. 19, 2020; Dec. 16, 2021>
  (9) Where the amount of restoration funds is reduced as a result of covering the costs of restoration by proxy under Article 37(9) of the Act, the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, etc., shall require that the reduced amount be re-deposited in accordance with Article 38 of the Act. <Amended on Aug. 22, 2012; Jun. 2, 2020; Aug. 19, 2020; Dec. 16, 2021>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 7, 2010]

Article 46 (Deposit of restoration funds) (1) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as where the area intended for conversion of a mountainous district is less than 660 square meters" in the proviso of Article 38(1) of the Act means any of the following cases: <Amended on Aug. 5, 2005; Feb. 1, 2007; Jul. 27, 2007; Jul. 24, 2008; Apr. 20, 2009; Nov. 26, 2009; Dec. 7, 2010; Jan. 28, 2011; Aug. 22, 2012; Nov. 11, 2015; Dec. 30, 2016; Oct. 30, 2018; Oct. 30, 2018; Dec. Jun. 7, 2023; May 7, 2024; Mar. 11, 2025>
  1. In cases where the area intended for the conversion or temporary use of a mountainous district is less than 660 square meters; provided, this shall not apply where the area has been subdivided to less than 660 square meters for the purpose of exemption from the obligation to deposit restoration funds;
  2. Where a project involves the installation of any of the following facilities or industrial complexes, implemented by the State, a local government, a public corporation, a quasi-governmental institution, a local government-invested public corporation, or a local government public corporation (excluding golf courses under Article 10(1)1 of the Installation and Utilization of Sports Facilities Act):
  a. Facilities under subparagraph 2 or 3 of Article 10 of the Act;
  b. Facilities under Article 12(1)8 of the Act;
  c. Facilities under Article 12(2)5 of the Act;
  d. Public facilities under subparagraph 13 of Article 2 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
  e. Transmission facilities (including access roads) under Article 10(4)3;
  f. Facilities under subparagraphs 1 a through n of Appendix 5 (excluding facilities under subparagraphs a through d of this subparagraph);
  3. In cases of projects for installation of facilities specified in any item of subparagraph 2, which are implemented by private business entities and are donated or transferred free of charge to the State or local governments;
  4. In cases of notifications of the temporary use of mountainous districts for the purpose of installing forest roads, work roads, forest product transport roads, or forest trails such as walking paths, exploration routes, hiking trails, firebreaks, or forest protection facilities;
  5. In cases where a person intends to temporarily use mountainous districts for any of the following purposes without altering the land characteristics of the mountainous districts, felling or excavating standing trees:
  a. Livestock grazing;
  b. Buried heritage surface survey under the Act on Protection and Inspection of Buried Heritage;
  c. Cultivation of items eligible for support as income sources for forest products under Article 8(1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Forestry and Mountain Villages Development Promotion Act;
  d. Piling up goods;
  5-2. Where the temporary use of a mountainous district involves the felling of standing trees for the cultivation of nut or medicinal plant species that are among the items eligible for support as income sources from forest products under Article 8(1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Forestry and Mountain Villages Development Promotion Act (limited to the cultivation of tall tree species such as chestnut, persimmon, and Korean pine);
  6. In cases of seeking permission for extraction of earth and stones in accordance with Article 37(2)2;
  7. In cases where a public corporation listed in each subparagraph of Article 17 of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Funeral Services installs a tree burial forest.
  8. Where a person intends to temporarily use mountainous districts for the investigation or excavation of the remains of fallen soldiers pursuant to Article 9 of the Act on the Excavation of the Remains of Soldiers Killed in the Korean War.
  (2) In accordance with Article 38 (3) of the Act, the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, etc. shall each year recalculate the restoration costs and require relevant person to deposit the difference between the initially deposited amount of restoration costs and the recalculated restoration costs; provided, where a person obligated to deposit the restoration costs under Article 38 (1) or (2) of the Act requests to deposit in advance the amount estimated to be additionally deposited annually during the period of mountainous district conversion, etc. the person may be permitted to deposit the amount calculated in accordance with the standards determined and publicly notified by the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service. <Added on Aug. 22, 2012; Nov. 11, 2015; Mar. 11, 2025>
  (3) The Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, etc. may require a person who meets all the following requirements to deposit restoration costs in installments in accordance with Article 38(4) of the Act, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs: <Amended on Aug. 22, 2012; Mar. 23, 2013>
  1. Where a person intends to deposit the restoration costs in cash;
  2. Where the content of a written application for permission for the conversion of mountainous districts, etc. shall correspond to all of the following items:
  a. The period for conversion of mountainous districts shall be 3 years or longer;
  b. The conversion of mountainous districts shall be implemented on a yearly basis;
  c. The area of mountainous districts subject to conversion, etc. shall be at least 100,000 square meters.

Article 46-2 (Interim restoration) (1) In any of the following cases, the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, etc. may order a person who is required to restore a mountainous district to perform interim restoration under the main clause, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 39(2) of the Act: In such cases, an interim restoration order shall be issued in writing, specifying the details, period, etc. of measures, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs: <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Dec. 7, 2010; Aug. 22, 2012; Mar. 23, 2013; Sep. 24, 2014; Oct. 30, 2018; Jan. 30, 2026>
  1. In cases where the period of permission or notification, etc. specified in any of the subparagraphs of Article 37(1) of the Act is 3 years or longer;
  2. In cases where protection of mountainous landscapes such as in visually exposed roadside areas;
  3. In cases where there is concern about forest disasters such as landslides.
  (2) In Article 39(2)1 of the Act, "areas prescribed by Presidential Decree" means 300,000 square meters. <Added on Sep. 24, 2014>
  [This Article Added on Jul. 27, 2007]

Article 47 (Exemption from restoration obligation) In Article 39(3)2 of the Act, "cases where there is no land to be restored, etc., as prescribed by Presidential Decree" means any of the following cases: <Amended on Aug. 5, 2005; Feb. 1, 2007; Jul. 27, 2007; Jul. 24, 2008; Apr. 20, 2009; Dec. 7, 2010; Jan. 28, 2011; Aug. 22, 2012; Nov. 11, 2015; Dec. 30, 2016; Jun. 2, 2017; Oct. 30, 2018; Jul. 2, 2019; May 7, 2024>
  1. Mountainous districts subject to restoration under Article 39(1) of the Act that can be utilized as forest roads, work roads, or forest paths such as walk trails, hiking trails, or exploration routes, in connection with forest management or forest-related public interest; provided, this shall not apply to mountainous districts that include cut or embanked slopes;
  2. Deleted; <Jul. 27, 2007>
  3. Where a mountainous district has been converted for the purpose of changing its land category, and there is no site subject to restoration, such as cut or embanked slopes;
  4. Where a mountainous district is temporarily used for any of the following purposes without altering its land characteristics (including logging of standing trees or excavation or extraction):
  a. Livestock grazing;
  b. Buried heritage surface survey under the Act on Protection and Inspection of Buried Heritage;
  c. Cultivation of items eligible for support as income sources for forest products under Article 8(1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Forestry and Mountain Villages Development Promotion Act;
  d. Piling up goods;
  4-2. In cases involving the felling of trees, cultivation of fruits or medicinal plants among the items eligible for support as sources of income for forest products under Article 8(1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Forestry and Mountain Village Promotion Act (limited to cultivation of trees such as chestnuts, persimmons, and pine nuts);
  5. Where a person who has obtained permission for conversion or temporary use of a mountainous district or has notified the conversion or temporary use of a mountainous district is re-granted permission for conversion or temporary use of a mountainous district or the notification of the conversion or temporary use of a mountainous district he or she has filed is accepted, before any measures under the subparagraphs of Article 41 of the Act are taken, and it is deemed unreasonable to restore the mountainous district whose topography has been altered for the intended project. In such cases, exemption from the restoration obligation shall be granted only once;
  6. Deleted; <Dec. 16, 2021>
  7. Where, in the course of converting or temporarily using a mountainous district, earth and stones are incidentally generated and extracted under a permit for earth and stones extraction, and such extraction is completed prior to the termination of the conversion or temporary use, and it is deemed unreasonable to restore the land before the conversion or temporary use of a mountainous district is concluded. In such cases, the exemption from the restoration obligation shall be limited to the obligation to restore the area covered by the earth and stones extraction permit under Article 39(1)2 of the Act.

Article 48 (Approval of restoration design plans) "Period prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 40(1) of the Act means any of the following periods: <Amended on Jul. 27, 2007; Dec. 7, 2010; Nov. 11, 2015; Oct. 30, 2018; Jun. 2, 2020; Aug. 19, 2020; Dec. 16, 2021>
  1. In cases of seeking approval for restoration design plans for restoration work before the expiration of the period of mountainous conversion, etc., the period prior to commencing the restoration work;
  2. In cases of seeking approval for a restoration design plan to carry out restoration work after the expiration of the period for the conversion, etc. of a mountainous district, the relevant period shall be deemed to be the period prior to such expiration;
  3. In cases of receiving an order to take measures under Article 37(7) of the Act or an interim restoration order under Article 39(2) of the Act (including cases applied mutatis mutandis under article 44(3) of the Act), a period of 30 days from the date of receiving the order for measures, etc.

Article 48-2 (Subjects to supervision for restoration works of mountainous districts) In the main clause, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 40-2(1) of the Act, "areas prescribed by Presidential Decree" means the permitted, notified, or designated areas classified in each of the following subparagraphs. In such cases, if a person obligated to perform restoration has obtained multiple permits or designations, or filed multiple notifications for adjacent mountainous districts for a project that is recognized as having the same purpose, the area shall be calculated by aggregating the areas of the permitted, designated, or notified forest mountainous districts to the extent that the uniformity of project purpose is recognized: <Amended on Jun. 2, 2020>
  1. In cases of receiving permission for conversion or temporary use of a mountainous district: 10,000 square meters;
  2. In cases of filing a notification of the conversion or temporary use of a mountainous district, which falls under Article 15(1)3 or 15-2(4) 3 of the Act: 10,000 square meters;
  3. In cases of receiving a permit for extraction of earth and stones for rocks: 50,000 square meters;
  4. In cases of receiving permission for earth and stones extraction: 10,000 square meters;
  5. In cases of designation of a quarry complex: 200,000 square meters.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Nov. 11, 2015]

Article 49 (Exemption from deposit of defect repair guarantee deposit) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 42(2) of the Act means any of the following cases: <Amended on Jul. 24, 2008; Dec. 7, 2010>
  1. Where the State, a local government, a public corporation, a quasi-governmental institution, a local government-invested public corporation, or a local government public corporation intends to undergo an inspection for completion of restoration works;
  2. If the amount of the defect repair warranty is less than 1 million won.

Article 49-2 (Investigation of illegally converted mountainous districts) In Article 44-2(2) of the Act, the "a specialized mountainous district institution prescribed by Presidential Decree" means the Korea Forest Conservation Association.
  [This Article Added on Dec. 7, 2010]

Article 50 (Designation of specialized institutions for recovery) (1) In Article 45(2) of the Act, "Requirements prescribed by Presidential Decree" means the following requirements: <Amended on Aug. 5, 2005; Aug. 4, 2006; Feb. 29, 2008; Jul. 24, 2008; Apr. 20, 2009; Dec. 7, 2010; Mar. 23, 2013; Nov. 27, 2018>
  1. There shall be at least 1 forest professional engineer, 1 civil engineer qualified under the National Technical Qualifications Act, and 1 forest engineering technician according to Appendix 3 of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Promotion and Management of Forestry Technology; provided, in the case of a corporation that intends to perform only the work specified in Article 45(1)1 and 2 of that paragraph, there shall be at least 1 forest professional engineer and 1 forest engineering technician;
  2. It shall have equipment prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs.
  (2) Where a person who meets the requirements under each subparagraph of paragraph (1) intends to be designated as a specialized institution for recovery under Article 45(2) of the Act, he or she shall submit an application for designation as an institution specialized in recovery to the Minister of the Korea Forest Service, along with documents prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>
  (3) The Administrator of the Korea Forest Service shall, upon receipt of an application for designation as a specialized institution for recovery pursuant to paragraph (2), examine as to whether it satisfies the requirements for designation specified in paragraph (1) and determine whether to designate it.

CHAPTER V SUPPLEMENTARY PROVISIONS

Article 50-2 (Payment of rewards) (1) The monetary rewards under Article 46-2 of the Act shall be paid in accordance with the criteria for payment of monetary rewards specified in Appendix 8-4, within budgetary limits. <Amended on Jun. 2, 2017>
  (2) The monetary rewards under paragraph (1) shall be granted only where a person has reported or accused a violator subject to report or accusation under Article 46-2 of the Act to the competent authorities or an investigative agency before such violator is discovered by an administrative agency, and where, with respect to such accusation or report, the prosecutor files an indictment, grants a stay of prosecution, or suspends the indictment, or where a judicial police officer suspends the investigation (limited to suspension due to the suspect). <Amended on Dec. 29, 2020>
  (3) In the cases where 2 or more persons jointly receive monetary rewards under paragraph (1), the distribution methods, other payment methods, procedures, etc. of the monetary rewards shall be determined by Decree of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>
  [This Article Added on Jul. 27, 2007]

Article 50-3 (Scope of affairs of persons responsible for site management business) (1) The scope of affairs of persons responsible for site management business under Article 46-3(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "on-site management officer") shall be as follows:
  1. Matters related to ensuring safety at earth and stones extraction sites;
  2. Matters related to the prevention of forest damage to the earth and stones extraction sites;
  3. Matters related to measures to prevent natural disasters at the earth and stones extraction sites;
  4. Matters related to the reduction of damage from earth and stones extraction, such as an interim recovery plan of an earth and stones extraction site;
  5. Matters related to safety education and disaster prevention education for people engaged in earth and stones extraction;
  6. Other matters related to safety and disaster prevention at the earth and stones extraction sites.
  (2) The deadlines for notification of designation of, and modifications to, on-site management officers shall be as follows:
  1. Where an on-site management officer has been designated: Within 30 days from the date of obtaining the earth and stones extraction permit, the date of quarry notification, or the date of acquiring or receiving earth and stones by purchase or gratuitous transfer;
  2. In cases of changing the on-site management officers: Within 30 days from the date of changing the on-site management officers.
  (3) In cases where a person specified in any subparagraph of Article 46-3(1) of the Act designates or changes an on-site management officer, he or she shall file a notification to the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service, etc. in the form prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs, attached with a certificate of employment of the on-site management officer.
  (4) In the proviso of Article 46-3(2) of the Act, "a case prescribed by Presidential Decree including a case where the same business entity consecutively obtains permission for extraction of earth or stone" means any of the following cases: <Added on Oct. 17, 2017>
  1. In cases where the same business entity receives a permit for earth and stones extraction in accordance with Article 25(1) of the Act;
  2. In cases where the same business entity has filed 2 or more quarrying notifications in accordance with Article 30(1) of the Act in the same quarry complex;
  3. In cases where the same business entity purchases or receives free donation of earth and stones in accordance with Article 35(1) of the Act.
  [This Article Added on Sep. 25, 2015]

Article 50-4 (Training institutions for on-site management officers) In the main clause of Article 46-3 (3) of the Act, "an institution prescribed by Presidential Decree" means an institution that falls under any of the following subparagraphs: <Amended on Oct. 17, 2017; Nov. 24, 2020; Mar. 11, 2025>
  1. Korea Quarrying Association;
  2. Korea Forest Conservation Association;
  3. Other corporations recognized and publicly notified by the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service as training institutions for on-site management officers.
  [This Article Added on Sep. 25, 2015]

Article 50-5 (Training period for on-site management officers) (1) On-site management officers shall receive at least 34 hours of new training necessary to perform their duties within 6 months from the date of designation or modifications thereof under Article 46-3(1) of the Act.
  (2) If a site management officer who received new training under paragraph (1) is designated or modified as an on-site management officer at another earth and stones extraction site within 2 years, he or she shall be deemed to have received new training under paragraph (1).
  (3) On-site management officers who have received new training under paragraph (1) or are deemed to have received new training under paragraph (2) shall receive at least 21 hours of continuing education within 6 months before and after the date every 2 years elapse from the date of completion of new training (in the case of field management officers specified in paragraph (2), referring to the date of receiving the original new training).
  (4) The education under paragraphs (1) and (3) shall include the following matters:
  1. Matters related to disaster prevention and safety management at the earth and stones extraction sites;
  2. Matters related to reducing environmental damage from the earth and stones extraction sites and other similar matters;
  3. Matters related to the systems and technologies for restoration of the earth and stones extraction sites;
  4. Matters related to the system and policies of earth and stones extraction;
  5. Matters related to earth and stones extraction technology.
  (5) In the proviso of Article 46-3(3) of the Act, "cases prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as cases where a person ... has completed education under Article 7 of the Mining Safety Act" means cases where a person designated or changed for designation as an on-site management officer under Article 46-3(1) of the Act has completed education under Article 7(2) of the Mining Safety Act and Article 8(2)2 or 3 of the Enforcement Decree of that Act by the time specified in each of the following subparagraphs: <Added on Nov. 24, 2020>
  1. In case of new or changed designation as an on-site management officer: Within 6 months from the date of designation or changed designation as an on-site management officer;
  2. In case of being engaged in the affairs as an on-site management officer: Within 6 months before and after the 2nd anniversary of the date of completion of new training (the original date of new training for on-site management officers specified in paragraph (2)).
  (6) The scope of education that can be exempted under the proviso of Article 46-3(3) of the Act shall be the education specified in paragraph (4)1. <Added on Nov. 24, 2020>
  (7) A person who falls under any of the subparagraphs of Article 46-3(1) of the Act shall pay the cost of textbooks, lecture fees, and other expenses necessary for training on-site management officers to the training institutions for on-site management officers under Article 50-4. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2016; Nov. 24, 2020>
  [This Article Added on Sep. 25, 2015]

