ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 18108, Sep. 29, 2003>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on October 1, 2003.
Article 2 (Applicability to restrictions on activities within mountainous districts for forestry use)
(1) The provisions of Article 12(3) and (4) shall begin to apply to the applications for permission for the conversion of mountainous districts for forestry use after this Decree enters into force.
(2) The provisions of Article 12(4) shall not apply to the area (including the area converted after this Decree enters into force at the request of permission for conversion filed before this Decree enters into force) converted from the land of production forest under Article 16(1) of the previous Forestry Act in order for farmers, foresters, and fishers to construct houses and their appurtenant facilities for the purpose of running agricultural, forestry, and fishery business before this Decree enters into force.
Article 3 (Transitional measures regarding conversion of conservation forest land)
Where an application for permission, consultation, etc. falling under any of the following subparagraphs is filed as at the time this Decree enters into force, the criteria for and restrictions of such permission, consultation, etc. shall be governed by the previous Enforcement Decree of the Forestry Act:
1. Permission for the conversion of conservation forest land under the previous provisions of Article 18(1) and (2) of the Forestry Act;
2. Consultation on designation, etc. of a district, zone, area, etc. under the previous provisions of Article 18(3) of the Forestry Act;
3. Sale, gratuitous concession, etc. of earth and stones under the previous provisions of Article 87(1) of the Forestry Act;
4. Permission for, or notification of, alteration of land characteristics of the forests under the previous provisions of Article 90 of the Forestry Act;
5. Permission for quarrying under the previous provisions of Article 90-2 of the Forestry Act;
6. Notification of quarrying in a quarry complex in accordance with the previous provisions of Article 90-5 of the former Forestry Act;
7. Permission for, or notification of, extraction of earth and sand under the previous provisions of Article 90-6 of the Forestry Act.
Article 4 (Transitional measures regarding substitute forest resource development charges)
(1) The standard unit price for the imposition of substitute afforestation expenses publicly notified by the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service under Article 24-2(5) of the previous Enforcement Decree of the Forestry Act as at the time this Decree enters into force shall be deemed the amount per unit area of the substitute forest resource development charges publicly notified by the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service under Article 24(4).
(2) The reduction or exemption of substitute afforestation fees shall be governed by the previous provisions with respect to an application for permission for the conversion of conservation forest land or permission for the alteration of land characteristics of the forest (including authorization, permission, etc. under which permission for the conversion of conservation forest land or permission for alteration of the land characteristics of the forest is deemed granted under other statutes), or a notification of alteration of land characteristics of the forest, filed before this Decree enters into force.
Article 5 (Transitional measures regarding quarrying permits and earth and sand extraction permits in visibly exposed areas along local roads)
In the cases where a person who received a quarrying permit or an earth extraction permit within 500 meters from a roadside area of a local road before May 16, 2000 intends to continue quarrying or extraction of earth in the area adjacent to the permit area, the provisions of Article 36(3)4c (including the case stipulated in Article 43(3)) shall not apply. <Amended on Aug. 5, 2005>
Article 6 Omitted.
Article 7 (Relationship with other statutes and regulations)
Any citation of the former Enforcement Decree of the Forestry Act or any provisions thereof in any other statutes or regulations as at the time this Decree enters into force shall be deemed a citation of this Decree or the corresponding provision thereof, if such corresponding provision exists.

