ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 22513, Dec. 7, 2010>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation; provided, the amended provisions of Articles 20-2 through 20-4 and Article 48-2 shall enter into force on July 1, 2011.
Article 2 (Temporary special cases concerning illegally converted mountainous districts)
(1) Facilities for common use or public use referred to in Article 2(1)2 of the Addenda to the Mountainous Districts Management Act, partially amended by Act No. 10331, (hereafter referred to as the "amended Act" in this Article) shall be as follows:
1. Facilities under subparagraphs 2 and 3 of Article 10 of the Act;
2. Facilities under Article 12(1)8 of the Act;
3. Facilities under Article 12(2)5 of the Act;
4. Public facilities under subparagraph 13 of Article 2 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act.
(2) The facilities for agriculture, forestry, and fisheries under Article 2(1)2 of Addenda to the amended Act shall be as follows:
1. Facilities under subparagraphs 4 and 5 of Article 10 of the Act;
2. Facilities under Article 12(1)2 through 5 of the Act;
3. Facilities under subparagraphs 10 through 12 of Article 2 of the Act on the Prevention of and Countermeasures against Agricultural and Fishery Disasters;
4. Facilities (including land) used for cultivating crops or growing perennial plants in accordance with the Agricultural Land Act;
5. Facilities (including land) used for the cultivation of perennial improved pasture grass and forage crops under the Grassland Act.
(3) In Article 2(2) of the Addenda to the amended Act, "mountainous districts that meet the standards prescribed by Presidential Decree" means the mountainous districts that meet all of the following standards:
1. It shall not be a mountainous district subject to an order to remove structures or to restore altered land characteristics under Article 44(1) of the Act;
2. It shall meet the standards for notification of conversion of mountainous districts under Article 15(2) of the Act or the standards for permission for conversion of mountainous districts under Article 18 of the Act; provided, if it is deemed that it is significantly unreasonable to apply such standards, the standards may be partially relaxed and applied as prescribed and publicly notified by the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service;
3. The mountainous districts to be notified shall be those owned by the applicant (only applicable to cases of using the facilities under paragraph (2));
4. It shall be used by a person qualified to acquire agricultural land under the Farmland Act (only applicable to cases where facilities under paragraph (2)4 are being used).
(4) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu receives a report on an illegally converted mountainous district under Article 2 of the Addenda to the amended Act, they may conduct an examination by means of reading aerial photographs, on-site inspection, hearing opinions of relevant persons, etc.
(5) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu has completed an examination under paragraph (4), they shall notify the applicant of the results of the examination in writing. In such cases, if a change in land category is required based on the examination results, the dispositions necessary for the change in land category shall also be notified.
(6) The detailed procedures for notification, examination, and notification of other illegally converted mountainous districts shall be determined and publicly notified by the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service.
Article 3 (Applicability to consultation on designation and determination of the areas, etc.)
(1) The amended provisions of the latter part of Article 6(1) and Appendix 2 shall begin to apply to the requests for consultations on designation and determination of the areas, etc. made to the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service after this Decree enters into force.
(2) In cases where consultations with the Administrator of the Korea Forest Service are underway regarding matters that do not change the surface area of the areas, etc. designated or determined at the time of enforcement of this Decree and where the mountainous district conversion area is less than 10 percent, the previous regulations shall apply.
Article 4 (Applicability to criteria for permission for conversion of mountainous districts)
The amended provisions of Appendix 4 shall begin to apply to the applications for permission for conversion of mountainous districts filed after this Decree enters into force.
Article 5 (Applicability to boundary marking for notification of conversion of mountainous districts)
The amended provisions of the latter part of Article 17(1) (including cases applied mutatis mutandis under Article 18-3(1) shall begin to apply to the notifications of conversion or temporary use of mountainous districts filed after this Decree enters into force.
Article 6 (Applicability to installment payment and reduction or exemption of substitute forest resource development charges)
The amended provisions of Article 21(2)6 and Appendix 5 shall begin to apply to applications for permission for conversion or temporary use of mountainous districts, or requests for consultation for administrative dispositions by which permission for conversion or temporary use of mountainous districts are deemed granted or excluded under other statutes after this Decree enters into force.
Article 7 (Transitional measures regarding temporary use of mountainous districts)
Where, at the time of the enforcement of this Decree, procedures for filing a notification of temporary use of a mountainous district are underway for the installation of facilities under the amended provisions of Article 12(5)1d, the previous provisions shall apply, notwithstanding the amended provisions.
Article 8 (Transitional measures upon delegation of authority)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 52(1), (3), and (7), the previous provisions shall apply to administrative procedures in progress, as of the time this Decree enters into force, with respect to administrative affairs for which the delegated authority has been changed.
Article 9 Omitted.

