35374
ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 35374, Mar. 11, 2025>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability to deliberation by Central Mountainous District Management Committee)
The amended provisions of Article 24(4), subparagraph 4-2 of Article 27, and Article 29-2(1)1e shall begin to apply to cases in which the amount per unit area of substitute forest resource development charges is determined and publicly notified after this Decree enters into force.
Article 3 (Applicability to installation conditions for facilities subject to reporting on temporary use of mountainous districts)
(1) The amended provisions of subparagraph 3b of Appendix 3-3 shall also apply to cases where, prior to the enforcement of this Decree, a notification of temporary use of mountainous districts has been filed pursuant to Article 17(1) as applied mutatis mutandis under Article 18-3(1), or where consultation has been requested for administrative disposition deemed as a notification of temporary use of mountainous districts pursuant to Article 14(4) as applied mutatis mutandis under Article 15-2(8) of the Act, and a notification of change or a request for consultation for such change is made after the enforcement of this Decree.
(2) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of subparagraph 3b of Appendix 3-3, where, prior to the enforcement of this Decree, a written notification of temporary use of mountainous districts has been filed pursuant to Article 17(1), as applied mutatis mutandis under Article 18-3(1), or consultation has been requested in order to take an administrative disposition deemed as a notification of temporary use of mountainous districts under other Acts pursuant to Article 14(4), as applied mutatis mutandis under Article 15-2(8) of the Act, the former provisions shall govern.
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning installation conditions for facilities subject to reporting on conversion of mountainous districts)
(1) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of subparagraph 5a of Appendix 3, where, prior to the enforcement of this Decree, a written notification of the conversion of mountainous districts has been filed pursuant to the former part of Article 17(1), or consultation has been requested in order to take an administrative disposition deemed as a notification of the conversion of mountainous districts under other Acts pursuant to Article 14(4) of the Act, as applied mutatis mutandis under Article 15(5) of the Act, the former provisions shall govern.
(2) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of subparagraph 5a of Appendix 3, where, prior to the enforcement of this Decree, a written notification of the conversion of mountainous districts is filed pursuant to paragraph (1) and a written notification for the change thereof is filed after the enforcement of this Decree, or where consultation is requested pursuant to paragraph (1) prior to the enforcement of this Decree and a request for consultation for the change thereof is made after the enforcement of this Decree, the former provisions shall govern.
Article 5 (Transitional measures regarding criteria for permission for conversion of mountainous districts)
(1) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of items 1 and 2 of Appendix 4, where, prior to the enforcement of this Decree, an application for permission for the conversion of mountainous districts has been submitted pursuant to Article 15(1), or consultation has been requested in order to take an administrative disposition deemed as permission for the conversion of mountainous districts under other Acts pursuant to Article 14(4) of the Act, the former provisions shall govern.
(2) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of subparagraphs 1 and 2 of Appendix 4, where a written application for mountainous district conversion permit is filed pursuant to paragraph (1) prior to the enforcement of this Decree, and an application for change permit or notification for change is filed after this Decree enters into force, or where consultation is requested pursuant to paragraph (1) prior to the enforcement of this Decree and a request for consultation for change is made after this Decree enters into force, the former provisions shall govern.
Article 6 (Transitional measures concerning revocation of earth and stones extraction permits)
Where an application for a permit for extraction of earth and rock or a permit for change thereof has been filed pursuant to Article 25(1) of the Act, or an application for the designation of a quarry complex or for the changed designation has been filed pursuant to Article 29(1) of the Act prior to the enforcement of this Decree, the former provisions shall govern, notwithstanding the amended provisions of subparagraph 8 of Appendix 8.

